{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived","id":277992,"title":"Development Tease: Book of the Deceived","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-11T01:54:47-07:00","id":277992,"title":"Development Tease: Book of the Deceived","content":"Hi, gang! Sorry for as much radio silence as there's been on my end, but I'm happy to report that <i>Book of the Deceived </i>is in layout in time for the Halloween season, and that's appropriate since it contains some of the creepiest material you're likely to see for the <b>World of Darkness</b>. The tone of the book and its protagonists, the mystery-shrouded members of the so-called Lost Guild, starts with the one element that sits at the core of all Deceived being...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>The Temakh</b></span><br /> <br /> Almost all supernatural character creation rules for the World of Darkness instruct players to construct a mortal character with mortal traits first, and then apply the appropriate template. In the case of the Deceived, one supernatural trait breaks this rule: the mummy\u2019s accursed completing soul fragment, called the temakh.<br /> <br /> The seven temakhs are entities of a sort, existing both outside and within their servants. Long ago, they counted themselves among the very Shan\u2019iatu\u2014the guildmasters of the Akhem-Urtu. Each presided over a specific form of artistic and cultural expression. Accordingly, they sought out followers who were adept at these same crafts, guiding and growing and molding that talent to serve their will. This means a Deceived\u2019s temakh shaped her mortal traits almost as much as it continues to shape her supernatural ones.<br /> <br /> The temakhs are eternal and human no longer. They are not spirits, nor gods, nor ghosts, but discorporate and chthonic presences that find collective embodiment in those deathless souls still bound to them. The mummies of each temakh are the flesh and hands by which their shared and scattered master grasps the living world. Without their mummies, who knows what the temakhs would be? Perhaps unmoored souls, screaming silently in the solitude of unending blackness and time; perhaps something darker still. Connected to their former guild underlings in this unique way, the temakhs might witness and shape the living world as even the Judges of Duat dare not.<br /> <br /> As characters, a player's choice of temakh determines his Deceived\u2019s favored Attributes, favored Skill, and favored Vice... among other qualities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":277,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","user":"CAS","date":". 10-11-2014, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T02:08:11-07:00","id":278006,"title":"","content":"So the the Temakh are a third player in the game the Judges and the Devourer play? Sounds interesting- especially since they were once among the Shan'iatu.. It makes me wonder why only 7 among them have survived in this form, and whether the rest may be in a much more horrible condition... I like it :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T03:00:37-07:00","id":278038,"title":"","content":"Beautiful beautiful previews. Ah, I'm in rapture right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278006#post278006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the the Temakh are a third player in the game the Judges and the Devourer play? Sounds interesting- especially since they were once among the Shan'iatu.. It makes me wonder why only 7 among them have survived in this form, and whether the rest may be in a much more horrible condition... I like it :P</div> </div> </div> </div>There are only seven presumably because there were seven Shan'iatu per Guild, and these seven are the seven Shan'iatu of the Lost Guild (and were likely destroyed when the Guild was betrayed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T03:07:30-07:00","id":278047,"title":"","content":"I was pretty happy with the work I did for this book. One of the things that's hard to find opportunities to do is to develop really compelling mythology--you only get one shot at something like V:TM's Caine myth, for example. I had the good fortune to find an opportunity like that here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T03:21:20-07:00","id":278050,"title":"","content":"Nice old Mummy shoutout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T05:02:36-07:00","id":278073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278038#post278038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beautiful beautiful previews. Ah, I'm in rapture right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are only seven presumably because there were seven Shan'iatu per Guild, and these seven are the seven Shan'iatu of the Lost Guild (and were likely destroyed when the Guild was betrayed).</div> </div> </div> </div>what I meant was that if those Temakh are what happened to the Shan'iatu of the Lost Guild, in which state are the rest? Did they survived one way or another, like the seven? Are they in a better state? Or maybe worse? In short, what can we learn from the state of the Temakh about the rest of the Shan'iatu?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T05:07:55-07:00","id":278074,"title":"","content":"The whole point of Irem was to fuel some kind of ascension to the afterlife on the part of the Shan'iatu, as I read things in the corebook. It looks as if the Shan'iatu of the Lost Guild (or the Akhem-Urtu, if I'm reading that preview right) were not allowed in on that ascension, but instead remained firmly tied to the corporeal world.<br /> <br /> It'll be interesting to see what the book has to say on the matter though. The Shan'iatu have always been a fairly shadowy presence in Mummy, but they're clearly an inextricable part of the Deceived. Could provide a good excuse to dig a little deeper on the subject.<br /> <br /> Either way, we find out in under three weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T06:20:07-07:00","id":278096,"title":"","content":"My assumptions here are that the Sixth Guild's guildmasters weren't privy to the Rite of Return and...disagreed, maybe? So...the Shan'iatu/Arisen tore them up and banished them into an ephemeral state. Wanting revenge, the Temakh fused bits of their ethereal-selves into their underlings, creating the Deceived. But what were they deceived in? The Shuankhsen sound deceived more than anyone - or hell, the Arisen are certainly the most deluded.<br /> <br /> After I read the <b>Mummy </b>core I came up with a few ideas of creatures and beings I wanted to stat up, but I wanted to wait for some supplements to be released so that my ideas could stand on their own. One thing I came up with was a Mummy which no longer had a human soul but was inhabited each by a pack of demons. It's nice to see a similar idea show up here (or, it looks similar enough from this narrow glimpse).<br /> <br /> My campaign's major arc is about the mysteries of a crystal skull (yes). It'll eventually be revealed that it's the skull of one of the Shan'iatu - whom I think all ascended to Duat to submissively serve the Judges, so I'm not quite sure of the ramifications of the relic yet. So this whole Temakh thing will throw it for a loop, which is good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T09:41:46-07:00","id":278188,"title":"","content":"Very interesting the tease indeed. The Temakh calls into question the theory that the Shan'iatu are the Judges of Duat that number 42, if 7 Shan'iatu were left behind it would mean only 35 &quot;ascended&quot;(there was 7 for each of the 6 Guilds), but we have 42 Judges not 35.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T11:05:14-07:00","id":278223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278188#post278188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very interesting the tease indeed. The Temakh calls into question the theory that the Shan'iatu are the Judges of Duat that number 42, if 7 Shan'iatu were left behind it would mean only 35 &quot;ascended&quot;(there was 7 for each of the 6 Guilds), but we have 42 Judges not 35.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my first thought as well.<br /> <br /> Proof that maybe, just maybe, it pays to listen to the game's developer when he says the common theory is wrong. We'll see how far that goes, but I'm gonna offer a pre-emptive apology to CAS for disregarding his comments in regards to the mistake of assuming the Shan'iatu and Judges were one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T11:58:47-07:00","id":278275,"title":"","content":"Thanks for sharing such a tantalizing preview! I love how CAS and the other Mummy designers are constantly subverting mechanical assumptions in nWoD. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278047#post278047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was pretty happy with the work I did for this book. One of the things that's hard to find opportunities to do is to develop really compelling mythology--you only get one shot at something like V:TM's Caine myth, for example. I had the good fortune to find an opportunity like that here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cannot wait to read this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T12:12:21-07:00","id":278284,"title":"","content":"What I kind of love best about the timing of this is that I've been spending the last few days going over Mummy stuff, from the blogs to D.C., so when I found our tease(as well as the news about Deceived!), I was extremely ready for hype. And I have money, so I can buy stuff on time!<br /> <br /> And yes, Mummy's willingness to turn aspects of the World of Darkness on it's head is one of the big reasons this game is awesome, and I love seeing that philosophy continue on with the boogeymen of ancients.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T12:19:54-07:00","id":278289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278223#post278223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was my first thought as well.<br /> <br /> Proof that maybe, just maybe, it pays to listen to the game's developer when he says the common theory is wrong. We'll see how far that goes, but I'm gonna offer a pre-emptive apology to CAS for disregarding his comments in regards to the mistake of assuming the Shan'iatu and Judges were one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which begets the question: What happened to them?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T14:41:02-07:00","id":278352,"title":"","content":"By the way, I'm very intrigued as to what CAS means by Book of the Deceived containing some of the creepiest material we've seen in WOD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T16:40:14-07:00","id":278444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278223#post278223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was my first thought as well.<br /> <br /> Proof that maybe, just maybe, it pays to listen to the game's developer when he says the common theory is wrong. We'll see how far that goes, but I'm gonna offer a pre-emptive apology to CAS for disregarding his comments in regards to the mistake of assuming the Shan'iatu and Judges were one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That announcement always weirded me out, given that the Pale Brood's description is pretty explicit that at least one Shan'iatu became a Judge. Of course, it's perfectly possible that it was just an editing oversight, and that the fate of the Shan'iatu changed at some point during development.<br /> <br /> That said, the Temakh aren't proof positive that the Shan'iatu didn't become the Judges. It is suggested in the book that one theory is that the Shan'iatu were merely mortal humans with a great deal of occult knowledge and an entire civilisation to drive their spells. In that case, after destroying the seven who were to become the Temakh, it would have been possible to raise seven devotees into the ranks of the Shan'iatu so that they numbered 42 for when they ascended to become the Judges.<br /> <br /> I am inclined to go with the actual developer of the line though, when he says that didn't happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T18:19:56-07:00","id":278521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278444#post278444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That announcement always weirded me out, given that the Pale Brood's description is pretty explicit that at least one Shan'iatu became a Judge.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and I evidently have very different readings of &quot;the one who would become known as the Eater of Blood&quot; being a guy who engaged in &quot;spiritual exploration of the spaces between death and the vast nothingness that lies beyond even Duat.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T19:09:59-07:00","id":278534,"title":"","content":"Upon rereading, it doesn't explicitly say Unem-Sef was actually one of the Shan'iatu. Still, Unem-Sef is one of the Judges, his title is the Eater of Blood, and the Pale Brood's description makes him out to have been mortal at the height of Irem's power. The Pale Brood's use was then forbidden, save for those priests that served him. Sounds a lot like a Shan'iatu leading the Su-Menent guild.<br /> <br /> Why? What's your reading of the text?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T19:55:03-07:00","id":278538,"title":"","content":"Hey, Azahul. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, now that we're already onto Part II of the in-house chronicle (coming in <i>Deceived</i>), I think it's safe for me to out myself on my own red herring. Sort of.<br /> <br /> The short version is that you both have it right, in part. Az, you hit the nail on the head in that the corebook doesn't explicitly say that the figure referred to in the write-up was one of the Shan'iatu, and that's important, but you were just as right when you pointed out that it looks like more than a simple coincidence.<br /> <br /> And in the interests of providing something other than more vaguebooking, I'll confirm something pertinent here:<br /> <br /> None of the Shan'iatu who created the Arisen ended up as Judges after Irem's fall. The Judges of Duat existed (or &quot;existed&quot;) as part of that cabal's culture and cosmological paradigm from the start, and those workers who would go on to become Arisen were already familiar with (and feared) them long before being subjected to the Rite of Return.<br /> <br /> Discuss!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":277,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","user":"CAS","date":". 10-11-2014, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T20:01:32-07:00","id":278543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278444#post278444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That announcement always weirded me out, given that the Pale Brood's description is pretty explicit that at least one Shan'iatu became a Judge. Of course, it's perfectly possible that it was just an editing oversight, and that the fate of the Shan'iatu changed at some point during development.<br /> <br /> That said, the Temakh aren't proof positive that the Shan'iatu didn't become the Judges. It is suggested in the book that one theory is that the Shan'iatu were merely mortal humans with a great deal of occult knowledge and an entire civilisation to drive their spells. In that case, after destroying the seven who were to become the Temakh, it would have been possible to raise seven devotees into the ranks of the Shan'iatu so that they numbered 42 for when they ascended to become the Judges.<br /> <br /> I am inclined to go with the actual developer of the line though, when he says that didn't happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's complicated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T20:04:58-07:00","id":278544,"title":"","content":"Well, I suppose the obvious question is &quot;If Ahken-Urtu's guildmasters live on in the deceived, are the other Shan'iatu riding along with the other Arisen?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm clearly missing out on something regarding Unem-Sef. Wha?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-11-2014, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T20:06:11-07:00","id":278545,"title":"","content":"It certainly does make the fact that Arisen made by the same Shan'iatu can't use magic on one another seem a lot more significant.<br /> <br /> Also, I was not expecting those comments to get responses from the writers. I am in quite a happy place right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T20:15:12-07:00","id":278548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278544#post278544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm clearly missing out on something regarding Unem-Sef. Wha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go to the relics section and take a gander at the backstory of the Pale Brood uter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T20:17:55-07:00","id":278549,"title":"","content":"Just did. Weird I never thought much of that story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T20:19:41-07:00","id":278550,"title":"","content":"The Shaunkshen write-up in the corebook mentions <i>creating</i> 42 gods. Something I've been tossing around for a while is the idea that the Shan'iatu were servants of some kind of super beings that they later turned into gods.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the Judges were riding the Shan'iatu...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T21:22:29-07:00","id":278562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278538#post278538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the Shan'iatu who created the Arisen ended up as Judges after Irem's fall. The Judges of Duat existed (or &quot;existed&quot;) as part of that cabal's culture and cosmological paradigm from the start, and those workers who would go on to become Arisen were already familiar with (and feared) them long before being subjected to the Rite of Return.<br /> <br /> Discuss!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, your wording is interesting, because there are already time-travel elements in the game (Words of Dead Fury, mainly), so it could be possible for a Shan'iatu to become a Judge and then have always &quot;existed&quot;. It's not a theory I like all that much, but it's a possibility.<br /> <br /> But the paradox in question is that this person who went on to become Unem-Sef clearly existed during Irem's height, yet Unem-Sef existed in the culture's cosmology &quot;from the start&quot;. Now, my personal pet theory is that the cosmology came first, and the gods of said cosmology were only actually made at a later date. As Illuminated Minutia pointed out, the Shuankhsen write-up mentions the creation of 42 gods. It would be easy enough to invent myths about 42 Judges and instill a fear and worship of them into the subjugated population, and then only later bring these icons into &quot;true&quot; existence through the mass sacrifice rituals that birthed the Shuankhsen.<br /> <br /> The question is where this took place in respect to Irem's fall and the Rite of Return. Every Arisen knows, or thinks they knows at least, that they met their Judge in Duat during the Rite. We know the Shuankhsen were being created throughout this period in return for the power to forge the Judges. The White Jackal in D.C. remembers the streets deserted on the day he went to undergo the Rite, which means the mass sacrifices were certainly taking place before he became Arisen and went to meet his Judge.<br /> <br /> And yet the time line gets a bit wonky, because isn't there a theory that the Rite was enacted over a really long period of time? Would the Judges have existed &quot; properly&quot; in time to meet those Arisen that first went through the Rite? The answer, presumably, is yes because every Arisen did meet the Judges, but it all feels a bit hazy round the edges.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why the Shan'iatu would have needed those gods to be made though. The term &quot;created&quot; feels quite deliberate and distinct from any notion that they might have ascended to godhood themselves, so it's not clear if they were getting anything in return for this act of genesis. I have this general idea that they wanted to reach Heaven, rather than Duat, and so created 42 gods in Duat as a kind of payment so that they could climb the Ladder of Sutek. The Shuankhsen were given to Ammut for the power to make those gods, and then Irem itself would have been the final payment for their ascension, hence its disappearance from the world. Meanwhile, a constant tithe of Sekhem must be delivered to these Judges in order to keep their place in Duat secure, and so, presumably, also enable the Shan'iatu's continued existence in Heaven.<br /> <br /> It's possible, then, that the Judges were mortal subjects of the Shan'iatu and were raised up to divinity in order to become the embodiment of their culture's beliefs, while the Shan'iatu went on to live in paradise. Being Lords of Duat, they would be bound to serve Azar, and likely have some kind of uneasy relationship with Anpu. Although that is a big question lingering over the whole of it. There are gods above the Judges, and one of them clearly has an interest in Arisen. Where they figure into all this is hard to determine. Possibly the gatekeepers to whom 42 divine subjects were offered?<br /> <br /> Metaphysics makes my head hurt. That's the gist of my general theory on the state of Irem and the fates of everyone involved. Quite a few holes left in it though, so I'm pretty excited to see what Deceived has to say on the subject and how much of the above (if any) is correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T21:38:38-07:00","id":278575,"title":"","content":"Judges aren't Gods though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T21:45:19-07:00","id":278579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278575#post278575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Judges aren't Gods though.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I got, he isn't saying that the Judges are gods, but rather the 'byproduct' or shadow of the Shan'iatu's ascendance to godhood, not that they are gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T21:47:03-07:00","id":278580,"title":"","content":"It doesn't feel like the passage is discussing the Shan'iatu though. The term &quot;created&quot; makes it sound like they were giving godlike power to other beings, rather than becoming so themselves. And as the Temakh establish, not all the Shan'iatu ascended, so &quot;42 new gods&quot; becomes a strange number if it were the Shan'iatu becoming those gods.<br /> <br /> And if the Shuankhsen section isn't speaking about the Judges or the Shan'iatu, then it must be referring to another set of 42 divine beings that have not been referenced anywhere else in the game-line so far, and have not come up before or since. Seems a bit strange, when there's the 42 &quot;godlike&quot; Judges on hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T22:08:58-07:00","id":278585,"title":"","content":"Current theory: The process isn't complete yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T02:49:24-07:00","id":278692,"title":"","content":"My personal theory is that the Judges are false idols used by the Shian'iatu in order to advance their agenda, and that they used the ritual which created the Arisen in order to feed them enough Sekhem to make them real- and that they still need that energy in order to exist. I don't know why, but making up gods in order to create a process which would eventually make those &quot;gods&quot; real sounds &quot;in theme&quot;, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T03:30:18-07:00","id":278703,"title":"","content":"The true nature of the Judges and/or the fate of the Shan'iatu are of far less concern to me than matters relevant to actual play - how to use the Deceived in a game, etc.<br /> <br /> I hope/expect to see more of the latter than the former in the Book of the Deceived. Franky, I wouldn't see it as a problem if the Book didn't give us any &quot;insider&quot; information about the Judges and the Shan'iatu at all. We already have all the information we need to tell interesting stories. These games are meant to be played, not just theorized about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 10-12-2014, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T03:34:17-07:00","id":278706,"title":"","content":"And Mummy is a game about secrets and forgotten knowledge. Having some actual forgotten knowledge to give players serves an in-game function. It's not going to be relevant in every game, goodness knows it probably won't in mine, but there is a reason for this stuff to exist.<br /> <br /> Given that the Book of the Deceived is meant to have enough rules in it to make playing Deceived characters a viable option, I see no reason not to expect exactly what you're asking for. The metaphysics of the Mummy universe, if it comes up, is a nice bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T03:42:36-07:00","id":278710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278538#post278538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the Shan'iatu who created the Arisen ended up as Judges after Irem's fall. </div> </div> </div> </div>What an interesting way to phrase something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T07:25:30-07:00","id":278795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278538#post278538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the Shan'iatu who created the Arisen ended up as Judges after Irem's fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love being right(-ish?).<br /> <br /> When I first read through the core I assumed the Shan'iatu and Judges were separate beings. It wasn't until I went on the internet that I found out people had interpreted certain passages to mean the Shan'iatu became the Judges. I do think that they ascended into Duat, but only to serve the Judges.<br /> <br /> The only other way I might budge - until we know more info - is if someone posited that the Shan'iatu powered their Judges into divine ascension, overthrowing the old gods like Anpu and his brethren.<br /> <br /> How does all this relate to the Deceived, though? What is Ammut's disposition towards them? Clearly Ammut existed before any theoretical Shan'iatu ascension, right? And why do the Judges 'dare not' interfere in the mortal realm as the Temakh do? I would only ever have the Judges act 'through' their Arisen agents, but I guess I never thought, &quot;Why?&quot; Their tied to this world, right? Sekhem is drained from this world into Duat, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T11:03:04-07:00","id":278944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278289#post278289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which begets the question: What happened to them?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I hope there's not a solid answer to this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T11:41:44-07:00","id":278958,"title":"","content":"If you had told me that they would be able to create a game line with the sort of storied revelations that punctuate Mummy and it's awesome setting during the early development spoilers of the Mummy core. I would have said that CAS and co. might not be able to pull it off. But damn man, you all are killing it. Cannot wait to get my hands on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T22:54:56-07:00","id":279391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278958#post278958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">damn man, you all are killing it. Cannot wait to get my hands on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very, very much. This book's been a while in the pipe, but if it's any consolation, we're actually quite proud of the end result. Supplements like this are important in <i>traditional</i> game lines, rolled out the traditional way, so they're doubly important in lines that are conceived and structured the way ours is. I knew going in that we'd have the potential to create one of the strongest and most memorable supplements of the nWoD era; one of those sourcebooks that really expands the game it's for, deepening the world as it opens up story and player options.<br /> <br /> Malcolm touched on it earlier, but I know the rest of the team -- George, Heather, Moon, Michael, and myself -- feel exactly as he does. With the help of some more of that beautiful Sam Araya art that's established the look of the game so vividly until now, we think we just might have pulled it off. It'll be fun and interesting, regardless; we're confident of that much. But it might also be a truly great RPG book. We'll see.<br /> <br /> C.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T00:52:15-07:00","id":279435,"title":"","content":"All the anticipation is akin to how I felt between Orpheus supplements. That's a very good thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T06:24:19-07:00","id":279586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=278538#post278538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>None </b>of the Shan'iatu <b>who </b>created the Arisen <b>ended up as</b> Judges <b>after </b>Irem's fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why, but I've had an urge to bold the most important things :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T06:46:29-07:00","id":279597,"title":"","content":"are the Temakh more like a Decree or a Judge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T07:43:32-07:00","id":279618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=279586#post279586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know why, but I've had an urge to bold the most important things :P</div> </div> </div> </div>What I inferred was that obviously all the Shan'iatu who didn't create Arisen were Judges before Irem fell.<br /> <br /> That's what that statement means, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T08:19:11-07:00","id":279638,"title":"","content":"You guys, I think, are somehow making this really overcomplicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T10:23:04-07:00","id":279832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=279638#post279638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys, I think, are somehow making this really overcomplicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>but its fun! The best theory is the most complicated one! don't listen to Occam's Razor- the man was a Seer. Give in to chaos :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T10:45:33-07:00","id":279880,"title":"","content":"That's an... oddly compelling argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T11:59:42-07:00","id":279974,"title":"","content":"Wow. Thank you guys SO much. We asked for a treat, and man what a doozy! its oozing with things we can digest, while still keeping the mystery something we want to dig into. This book looks like its going to be a mind bomb. As for my theory.. Ive always felt the shaniatu were a senate, with replacement members. As such, the whole statement about the shaniatu creating mummies not becoming Judges makes sense--the shaniatu were replaced regularly, with the role being constant. I like the broken time theory--secrets ripped from skies is another utterance that shows off the wibbly wobbly that Mummy cosmology allows. And thats just a PC power. Even still, the devs have said before Judges are not gods, and the shaniatu created gods. We're slowly putting the puzzle together, and the amount of mystery generated now is far more interesting than our prior theory of Judges = Senate. Love this game, love the mystery. Thank you guys again for dropping in to say something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:01:13-07:00","id":280112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived#post277992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Connected to their former guild underlings in this unique way, the temakhs might witness and shape the living world as even the Judges of Duat <b>dare</b> not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, very interesting.<br /> <br /> The Judges are exceedingly remote to material reality as we understand it. The Arisen and relics seem to be the only way they can interact with the world. Previous I thought this was by either design or some sort of divine decree. Now I wonder if is out of fear.<br /> <br /> Fear of what might happen if they do meddle directly in our world perhaps? The questions is what could frighten a Judge? Surely only Ammut or one of the Nameless Gods. Maybe if the Judges get directly involved it might break some cosmic rule and let these other more dangerous entities also directly interact with our world...not a good thing for anyone. <br /> <br /> This requires some thought. Hopefully a more complete explanation of Mummy's metaphysics will be detailed in the final version of <i>Deceived </i>and rounded off in Dreams of Avarice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T18:05:23-07:00","id":280344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=280112#post280112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This requires some thought. Hopefully a more complete explanation of Mummy's metaphysics will be detailed in the final version of <i>Deceived </i>and rounded off in Dreams of Avarice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Sothis Ascends will probably be the last piece of the puzzle, considering it's going to cover Turn 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T19:44:11-07:00","id":280432,"title":"","content":"For some reason, my mind keeps going back to the description of the Pale Brood. Specifically, the line about the <i>mundi morior</i>, or &quot;diseased world&quot;, and the tunnels that run beneath it. It's worded a bit strangely, but if it does mean to refer to the physical world, the Twenty-Two Voices of Undoing could have something to do with the Judges' reluctance to interfere directly. The Eater of Blood in particular is intimately aware of the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T03:31:58-07:00","id":280786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=280344#post280344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Sothis Ascends will probably be the last piece of the puzzle, considering it's going to cover Turn 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't; Sothis starts in Turn 1, 1600-plus-change years after the Rite of Return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T03:53:51-07:00","id":280812,"title":"","content":"The perhaps minor, and I'm making too much of it, stuff that always keeps rolling around in my mind behind some of the metaphysical goings on in Mummy is the references to reaching beyond space and time and all that.I don't know if I'm simply going red herring on this with words to evoke a sort of Lovecraftian feeling or if there really will be something in that we see more of with the Deceived and other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T06:34:01-07:00","id":280937,"title":"","content":"Since the Deceived are experts at Name magic, I wonder if we'll see rules for the rumored &quot;sorcerers.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T06:45:38-07:00","id":280959,"title":"","content":"By the way, is the book only about the Deceived, or there is a chance that we will see more information about the Lifeless or other antagonists?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:16:26-07:00","id":281022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=280786#post280786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't; Sothis starts in Turn 1, 1600-plus-change years after the Rite of Return.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's always what I had assumed. I'm curious if all the book's chapters are just the Turns or if there's other information, and how much information will be given about the current Turn (possibly suggestions for the 3400ad Turn in a sidebar?).<br /> <br /> I should wait patiently for such questions until <b>Deceived</b> is out, but hey","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:27:15-07:00","id":281138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=280786#post280786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't; Sothis starts in Turn 1, 1600-plus-change years after the Rite of Return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang, I must have miscounted turns. Alas.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, side note, but I wonder how much of Irem's past is meant to stay a mystery and how much is designed and was just kept for later books? Like Decieved and Avarice will pretty clearly drop some canon info, but I wonder how much was built or inserted just to be mysterious puzzle pieces that we can just put together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T18:14:35-07:00","id":281766,"title":"","content":"I really am hoping there's some way for mortals, Arisen, and other non-Deceived to learn Deceived Name Magic. Both so that Sorcerers can have some mechanical backing, and as a temptation for my more heretical players to seek out and study.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T18:40:36-07:00","id":281788,"title":"","content":"Nah, leave Deceived Name Magic to the Deceived. It's their signature thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T18:47:10-07:00","id":281792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=281788#post281788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, leave Deceived Name Magic to the Deceived. It's their signature thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? I mean, Name Magic is described as being one half of all magic. Which logically includes that magic which was practiced before Irem fell, and therefore a magic probably used by mortals. Narratively, it makes the most sense for others to learn. It's the free-form experimental magic, so anyone mucking around with occult forces could pick up.<br /> <br /> Besides, a lot of Arisen stuff in the book so far (the White Jackal's Washington, some Sesha-Hebsu Utterances) are supposedly based on Name magic principles. I'd be pretty disappointed if there were no mechanics for that kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T22:23:24-07:00","id":281954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=281792#post281792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it? I mean, Name Magic is described as being one half of all magic. Which logically includes that magic which was practiced before Irem fell, and therefore a magic probably used by mortals. Narratively, it makes the most sense for others to learn. It's the free-form experimental magic, so anyone mucking around with occult forces could pick up.<br /> <br /> Besides, a lot of Arisen stuff in the book so far (the White Jackal's Washington, some Sesha-Hebsu Utterances) are supposedly based on Name magic principles. I'd be pretty disappointed if there were no mechanics for that kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I err on agreeing with Arcane. Nothing wrong with the idea of the forbidden magic some speak of in whispers and know some little bit about with the Deceived being the true purveyors of it, but that tends to be the feel I like to keep with that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:28:02-07:00","id":282276,"title":"","content":"I think some guidelines for the otherwise GM-fiat 'mortal sorcerer' rules would be cool, but I'm not sure if this would be the supplement for it.<br /> <br /> Can we get more teases, pretty please? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe it's obvious, but I'm wondering how 'Mummy-like' the Deceived are. Do they spend the majority of time in henet? Do they wake up for Sothic turns?<br /> <br /> I wonder about their Morality stat but that's kind of a big spoiler. I think answers to the above might have interesting implications. If they spend time in henet, I mean, do they even go to Duat? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:12:19-07:00","id":282344,"title":"","content":"Besides books like Mage, Witch Finders or Second Sight, how many more rulesets for mortal sorcerers do we need? I'd prefer (and expect) Mummy wordcount to actually focus on Mummy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T10:25:50-07:00","id":282442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=282344#post282344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides books like Mage, Witch Finders or Second Sight, how many more rulesets for mortal sorcerers do we need? I'd prefer (and expect) Mummy wordcount to actually focus on Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think people mentioned sorceres with Iremite magic because the corebook mentions them, but it don\u00b4t go in detail at all. I dunno how I fell about it. If there is space in the book I say sure go ahead, but I would rather have more details on the Amkhata or the Shaunksem or other possible forms of Lifeless if the book talks about something other than the Deceived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T11:08:32-07:00","id":282532,"title":"","content":"If I had to guess, I'd say that mortal sorcerers must collect relics (or sacrifice human lives) in order to amass the Sekhem needed to unleash Utterances. Only those who have died and have returned through Shan'iatu sorcery can collect their own personal reserves of Sekhem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T13:14:17-07:00","id":282627,"title":"","content":"Im on the bandwagon for mummy style iremite sorcerers. They were talked about in open dev, as well as mentioned frequently. Ive personally involved mortal sorcerers siince the core, hinting and teasing. But after reading Guildhalls (specifically the sesha hebsu section) it became clear that mortal sorcerers are considered heretics and likely pull the same stuff Deceived do. Im hoping that mortal sorcerers havent been revealed yet because theyre a deceived style character, minus tem-akh but probably similar mechanically to a backwards mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T15:05:47-07:00","id":282758,"title":"","content":"I'd be happy if Sorcerers get rules at some point. That being said, I'm also happy using fan created material for them. Namely Octavo's Second Sight hack (Disciples of Duat), which I used in my last Mummy Campaign. <br /> <br /> I was thinking that when I run my next Mummy game, if Sorcerer rules are not presented in the core MtC line that Witch Finders actually lets you build some pretty awesome Necromatic/Darkness/Fate (basic themes/focuses of Iremite Magic that we've seen so far) pretty easily and with a bit more &quot;kick&quot; as antagonists. <br /> <br /> As for the matter of where we might see them, I'd place more of a bet on Sothis Ascends. For a couple of reasons.<br /> <br /> Firstly, Iremite Sorcerers would have come along after the fall of Irem, some of the relics described in the core talk about how later ancient cultures got hold of a bit of Irems knowledge and ran with it (and often screwed up and caused &quot;bad stuff&quot;tm to happen). So I'd not be surprised if Iremite/Scorpion Sorcerers have their origins in Turn 1 of the Sothic Cycle. Likewise, I would not be surprised if their origin ties into the Arisen cults of that time. <br /> <br /> Secondly, the Deceived, I suspect are going to require a lot of word count to cover properly. As they have their own history and culture to flesh out. Not to mention an obviously quite different rule set and maybe the basics of a semi &quot;free form&quot; magic system ala Mage or Blood Sorcery. On top of that we know the book contains the second part of the Avarice Chronicle, which is likely to be around 20-30 pages. Basically, even though Deceived is supposed to be around 160 pages (I think from the old preview info) that's still a bit of a squeeze for the amount of info its got to cover. <br /> <br /> Thirdly, if I remember correctly from the interview CAS did about a year ago, Sothis Ascends is introducing at least a single new type of antagonist. Its a big book of setting but its also a bit of a tool kit for powers, relics and new antagonists from what he hinted at. Particularly, I think it was going to look at &quot;lesser&quot; immortals (likely all lifeless) that more &quot;modern&quot; ancient cultures tried to create using incomplete and flawed knowledge of the Rite of Return. So if that sort of stuff is making it into Sothis, it would make sense to throw in the Sorcerers as an additional Antagonist type at the same time. <br /> <br /> Actually, in relation to that third point, if memory serves Sothis Ascends was possibly going to involve at least some word count on the other two &quot;old school&quot; immortals: The Purified and Blood Bathers from WoD Immortals. I seem to remember one of the writers (Malcolm???) during the Kickstarter/preview core pdf discussions talking about how their was some stuff written about how the Purified see the Arisen (sorta like a stereotype sentence that we get for Vampires, Werewolves etc in most books when the splats are presented). It was pretty horrifying apparently. They may have also been a side-box style paragraph about the topic. This was nearly 2 years ago, so I am honestly not sure how much is accurate recall and how much is my mind filling in blanks/wish fulfillment. <br /> <br /> Got kinda sidetracked there...anyway, roll on Deceived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T16:03:22-07:00","id":282847,"title":"","content":"I wonder if we are going to get any more info about Duat either in Sothis or Deceived.<br /> The Book of Going Westward strech goal wasn\u00b4t achieved so I guess detailed information about the Judges would have to be in one of these books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T16:59:15-07:00","id":282936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=282344#post282344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides books like Mage, Witch Finders or Second Sight, how many more rulesets for mortal sorcerers do we need? I'd prefer (and expect) Mummy wordcount to actually focus on Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a few reasons, not the least of which is that <b>Mage</b> is a different game with different themes than <b>Mummy</b>, <b>Witch-finders</b> is for <b>Hunter</b>, and...I'm not the biggest fan of <b>Second Sight</b>.<br /> <br /> One of the bigger reasons, though, is how often mortal sorcerers are mentioned in the <b>Mummy </b>books as if they're expected to have their own rules:<br /> <br /> There's mention of them creating greater amkhata (which, admittedly, is detailed).<br /> <br /> Mortal sorcerers &quot;wield a fragment of [power]&quot; &amp; &quot;Sorcerers concentrated will and scholarship into an elementary command of Sekhem, so they deserve respect, though never friendship&quot; &amp; &quot;Sorcerers know something of the Will, so their creations may contain secrets that will allow scribes to revive the old magic&quot; (<b>Guildhalls</b>), and also page 86 of <b>Guildhalls</b> they're mentioned in a table on using talismans.<br /> <br /> The core talks about how Shuankhsen get a Descent reset when they eat 'sorcerers.' The core says Mummies can learn Utterances from sorcerers - something very specific to this game's rules. It also mentions sorcerers can summon Mummies from henet without relics, and that there's certain effects when a vestige is destroyed near a sorcerer. Many relics mention sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, one of the main recommended styles of <b>Mummy</b> play is a pyramid-like structure with one or two Mummies, probably a Sadikh, and then some cultists all as PCs. Providing rules for <b>Mummy</b>-specific mortal sorcerers would be a fun addition to that. Especially with this reason, it doesn't detract '<b>Mummy </b>wordcount' from 'actually focusing on <b>Mummy</b>' because it's still providing rules for PC play in the game, you know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":". 10-15-2014, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T17:06:05-07:00","id":282940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=282936#post282936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Sorcerers know something of the Will, so their creations may contain secrets that will allow scribes to revive the old magic&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That quote, incidentally, is why I'd like rules in the Book of the Deceived allowing mortals to use Deceived magic. The Will refers to the magic the Deceived are meant to practice, and we have tidbits like that one that indicate they're not the only ones who use it.<br /> <br /> As a result, the &quot;Name magic is the Deceived's schtick&quot; comments don't really ring true for me. There are clearly lost adherents of Deceived magic who were born after Irem's fall, and a short segment detailing how mortals and others might access Deceived magic would finally bring that aspect of the game to life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T20:26:06-07:00","id":283156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=282758#post282758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be happy if Sorcerers get rules at some point. That being said, I'm also happy using fan created material for them. Namely Octavo's Second Sight hack (Disciples of Duat), which I used in my last Mummy Campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aw shucks. I'm glad you got some use out of that!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=282936#post282936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thirdly, one of the main recommended styles of <b>Mummy</b> play is a pyramid-like structure with one or two Mummies, probably a Sadikh, and then some cultists all as PCs. Providing rules for <b>Mummy</b>-specific mortal sorcerers would be a fun addition to that. Especially with this reason, it doesn't detract '<b>Mummy </b>wordcount' from 'actually focusing on <b>Mummy</b>' because it's still providing rules for PC play in the game, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely a reason I'm looking forward to info and rules on Sorcerers. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T06:34:24-07:00","id":283808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>reseru:</b> When I first read through the core I assumed the Shan'iatu and Judges were separate beings. It wasn't until I went on the internet that I found out people had interpreted certain passages to mean the Shan'iatu became the Judges. I do think that they ascended into Duat, but only to serve the Judges. </div> </div> </div>What if they <i>were</i> beholden to the Judges, and Irem and the Arisen were the price of getting out from under them - &quot;here, have these servants instead.&quot; <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>CAS:</b> I knew going in that we'd have the potential to create one of the strongest and most memorable supplements of the nWoD era; one of those sourcebooks that really expands the game it's for, deepening the world as it opens up story and player options. </div> </div> </div>Well, the game as stands oozes atmosphere. The teaser is interesting in that it makes me wonder where these mummies fit into the Rite of Return. Did the Akhem-Urtu guildmasters contrive some way to perform it or have it performed? Or are the Deceived a different order of being altogether? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Hawthorn:</b> Fear of what might happen if they do meddle directly in our world perhaps? The questions is what could frighten a Judge? Surely only Ammut or one of the Nameless Gods. Maybe if the Judges get directly involved it might break some cosmic rule and let these other more dangerous entities also directly interact with our world...not a good thing for anyone. </div> </div> </div>Or maybe let something from our world into theirs? According to Menat's account, the Shan'iatu found a &quot;mouth&quot; in the desert, which some have interpreted as Ammut. Whether it is or not, is something already devouring this world, and is the passing of Irem into Duat meant to preserve something of it away from this devourer's reach? Relics drain energies - and Sekhem is an energy of emotional and experiential connection - life force in the sense of &quot;this life I have lived.&quot; Thus relics collect <i>meaning</i> out of the world and send it to Duat - what if that's to save it? And the Judges fear to act to directly in case they alert the devouring power to this pipeline? In a way, that would make the Shan'iatu the good guys, which is a pretty horrible thought. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Cleverest of Things:</b> Im on the bandwagon for mummy style iremite sorcerers. </div> </div> </div>Because their sorcery is said to be so different in approach from what the other books tend to focus on, so am I. Although I also favour there being a way for mummies to access it. But it's not something I'm desperate for, (If I was using any of the other books for it, I think I'd adapt relic-making from Reliquary for the creation of de-facto spells as well as lasting relics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T16:36:11-07:00","id":284343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=283808#post283808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if they <i>were</i> beholden to the Judges, and Irem and the Arisen were the price of getting out from under them - &quot;here, have these servants instead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=283808#post283808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe let something from our world into theirs? According to Menat's account, the Shan'iatu found a &quot;mouth&quot; in the desert, which some have interpreted as Ammut. Whether it is or not, is something already devouring this world, and is the passing of Irem into Duat meant to preserve something of it away from this devourer's reach? Relics drain energies - and Sekhem is an energy of emotional and experiential connection - life force in the sense of &quot;this life I have lived.&quot; Thus relics collect <i>meaning</i> out of the world and send it to Duat - what if that's to save it? And the Judges fear to act to directly in case they alert the devouring power to this pipeline? In a way, that would make the Shan'iatu the good guys, which is a pretty horrible thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>SOLD!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T22:09:48-07:00","id":284649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=283808#post283808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'd adapt relic-making from Reliquary for the creation of de-facto spells as well as lasting relics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a really cool idea. If I do find myself needing to represent sorcerers in-game before proper rules for them come out, that seems like a neat way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T05:48:24-07:00","id":284869,"title":"","content":"In thinking of the two concepts I was just 'sold' on I have to wonder how Ammut and the Shuankhsen come into this.<br /> <br /> In the first option, why would the Shan'iatu bargain with Ammut if they were trying to escape the rest of the Judges? Or did they think, &quot;Okay, just one last eldritch pact before we're free&quot; or, &quot;We're tricking her&quot;? When really, she tricked them since she turned the sacrifices into a 'long term investment' by creating her own Mummies?<br /> <br /> In the latter, why would they bargain with Ammut if she's the thing they're trying to save this world from? And is this world so fucked that the Shan'iatu seriously thought the best course of action was to create life energy-draining relics and hide them away in a demonic dimension? And ensuring this plot was successful by binding their servants' souls to decaying corpses for all eternity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T06:06:11-07:00","id":284894,"title":"","content":"&quot;The world is ultimately doomed&quot; certainly wouldn't be an out of the question sentiment in a setting with as many eldritch abominations running around as there are in Mummy.<br /> <br /> I'm less sure about the Shan'iatu making the Arisen in order to escape the Judges. The Judges are emblematic of Bronze Age justice, which the Shan'iatu imposed on their own civilisation. To me, that, more than anything, suggests a &quot;chicken and the egg&quot; scenario. Did the Shan'iatu impose laws on Irem because they were enslaved to creatures that thought these laws were proper, or did they &quot;create&quot; these Judges in the myths of the civilisation they made in order to have a divine authority to call upon when executing said laws. Given the hints in the Pale Brood's description and the section on the Shuankhsen, it sounds like the latter is a bit more likely.<br /> <br /> Mulling on the &quot;Shan'iatu are actually slaves to the Judges, and so created the Arisen to escape&quot; idea did turn up an amusing little thought though. Mummies can escape the Judges themselves by going through Apotheosis. If you were to accept that the Arisen were made as subsitutes for the slavery of the Shan'iatu, what if to achieve Apotheosis you have to do something similar? Suddenly Mummy is looking an awful lot like Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T06:28:42-07:00","id":284905,"title":"","content":"At the very least that'd be a great campaign hook: a bunch of heretical Mummies running around trying to create their replacements","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T14:57:41-07:00","id":285433,"title":"","content":"Funny how we all thought that the Shan'iatu becoming the judges was a scary idea, and yet every alternative theory that you guys have presented is even more eerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T20:47:17-07:00","id":287200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CAS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived#post277992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, gang! Sorry for as much radio silence as there's been on my end, but I'm happy to report that <i>Book of the Deceived </i>is in layout in time for the Halloween season, and that's appropriate since it contains some of the creepiest material you're likely to see for the <b>World of Darkness</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so, does it being in layout in time for the holiday season mean that we can expect a release before Halloween, or does it mean that it will have reached the layout stage by Halloween?<br /> <br /> I was kind of assuming the former, but upon rereading I realised that it doesn't actually give any indication of when the book might drop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T01:10:07-07:00","id":287334,"title":"","content":"Well... to play the guesstimation game.<br /> <br /> From last weeks Monday Meeting Notes, Mike Chaney noted that he was expecting the majority of the art back last week (meaning they should be in by now). However, he was also expecting the NPC portraits and possible splat pictures to come in this week. Considering Mr Chaney has said he's done the layout for the book and just needs to swap out placeholder art for the final ones, it seems like waiting on art is the main issue at the moment. <br /> <br /> So, best case scenario (by my reckoning, and I've been dead wrong at estimating these things several times in the past) we would see Deceived released on the Wednesday (the general release day now for Onyx Path) of the final week of October (so the 29th). However, that presuming all art has come in/will come in as expected and that the CCP and DriveThruRPG approvals takes about 48 hours between both of them (presuming the final version with art was submitted late on Friday of this week).<br /> <br /> We'll be able to make a more educated and less speculative guess after this weeks Monday Morning Meeting Notes are released in the next 24 hours. I'm not hedging my bets either way but at the moment it looks like the book could come out anytime from the final week of October at the earliest to the middle of November at the latest (so a week and a half to a month basically). If another accursed delay (plague of locusts that eat pdf files is my bet) occurs that time might stretch out to 6 weeks,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T06:16:21-07:00","id":287522,"title":"","content":"So I get to spend every Wednesday (well, Thursday, when accounting for time zones) for the next six weeks refreshing the webpage constantly? Beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T08:08:38-07:00","id":287641,"title":"","content":"Give it three weeks before you start doing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T11:18:37-07:00","id":287851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=287641#post287641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give it three weeks before you start doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this statement.<br /> <br /> I call it a guesstimation game for a reason. Its all just speculation based on what info we have. In no way treat it as a reliable forecast of how the books progress will continue from our current point in time. <br /> <br /> Nice to know someone else suffers from being across the Atlantic from Onyx Path's offices Azahul. All the good announcement and such happen while I'm sound asleep. Still gives me something nice to wake up to in the mornings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:58:23-07:00","id":288537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=287851#post287851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I second this statement.<br /> <br /> I call it a guesstimation game for a reason. Its all just speculation based on what info we have. In no way treat it as a reliable forecast of how the books progress will continue from our current point in time.<br /> <br /> Nice to know someone else suffers from being across the Atlantic from Onyx Path's offices Azahul. All the good announcement and such happen while I'm sound asleep. Still gives me something nice to wake up to in the mornings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things are picking up tough, acording to the Monday Morning Meetings it seens they want to do the cover this week, and expecting most of the art to be in by next week. I guess we can hope for a Haloween realese.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T08:31:34-07:00","id":288556,"title":"","content":"Down that road lies madness.<br /> <br /> I dunno if you guys followed the entire Flowers of Hell fiasco, but trust me: down that road lies madness.<br /> <br /> Give it at least three weeks before you start spam reloading on Wednesdays.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T11:15:04-07:00","id":288705,"title":"","content":"Nah, I've totally signed up for the hope it'll be released this month. Thanks for trying, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T11:29:44-07:00","id":288709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=288556#post288556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Down that road lies madness.<br /> <br /> I dunno if you guys followed the entire Flowers of Hell fiasco, but trust me: down that road lies madness.<br /> <br /> Give it at least three weeks before you start spam reloading on Wednesdays.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that expecting Sothis Ascends to be in editing by the end of the month, and Deceived,Sothis,The Anthology and Rio out by the end of the year is the definition of madness, right?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T13:09:03-07:00","id":288820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=288705#post288705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, I've totally signed up for the hope it'll be released this month. Thanks for trying, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>All I can say is &quot;Seriously, don't&quot;. What you do from there is your own spongecake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T13:49:03-07:00","id":288860,"title":"","content":"Wait, there's cake now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T13:53:41-07:00","id":288864,"title":"","content":"It's in Book of the Deceived.<br /> <br /> ...wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T14:00:03-07:00","id":288869,"title":"","co