orrect? So I'll have a good bit of forewarning before I'm able to get my own grubby mitts on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T18:26:12-07:00","id":289149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=289148#post289148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'll be released to the Kickstarter backers first, correct? So I'll have a good bit of forew arning before I'm able to get my own grubby mitts on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Deceived wasn't a Stretch goal, it was part of the regular schedule like Sothis Ascends.<br /> The missing strech goals are: Rio, a Fiction Anthology, a Novel and Dreams of Avarice(a in-setting prop)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T19:55:01-07:00","id":289187,"title":"","content":"True...we never did earn the Book of Going Westward. I'm hoping if the line proves popular enough we'll get it anyway. Followed by a 2nd ed (Chronicle), but I'd say the latter is years off.<br /> Meanwhile I eagerly await my mast- I mean the Deceived, traitors of Irem!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T20:14:29-07:00","id":289211,"title":"","content":"Now that it's officially announced as second edition I'm sure they'll want to do all the game-lines. As <b>Mummy </b>was the last one released before the new rules, and as they seem to be doing two updated games per year, I'd say <b>Mummy</b>'s second edition will be in 2017.<br /> <br /> I wonder what other supplements CAS had in mind beyond <b>Book of Going Westward</b>, but even these teases about the Deceived and Temakh make me think that said book of judges would be a lot more interesting than I initially thought a couple years ago","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T21:36:47-07:00","id":289229,"title":"","content":"Well, my interest is rekindled.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately my group has very little interest in playing a game based in 1st edition WoD rules, and I don't know if I could get most of them to buy into Mummy's premise and unique elements. So I haven't had much occasion to keep myself invested in checking here.<br /> <br /> But seeing that Book of the Deceived is finally coming along is a great help here. I should go look at the DC book I got for backing the Kickstarter but never opened...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T22:00:26-07:00","id":289255,"title":"","content":"You will quite like it, I promise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T23:05:38-07:00","id":289282,"title":"","content":"Man, if we don't get the Book of Going Westward I'm going to be even more sad I didn't contribute to the Kickstarter. Would be a true shame.<br /> <br /> The tragic thing, I guess, about the World of Darkness Second Edition is that Mummy feels like the first game to actually nail the first edition nWoD. By which I mean that, of all the game-lines I've looked at, it's the most consistent mechanically. Nearly all the powers are useful, and don't require other powers as prerequisites. There are very few cases where I've not been able to work out how something is meant to work. I haven't yet encountered anything truly bizarre, like Changeling having an entire section dedicated to how Dreams work and a Contract of Dreams that includes only two Clauses that can be used in Dreams, one of which ignores the Dream mechanics entirely.<br /> <br /> It feels, for want of a better word, &quot;balanced&quot;. Not as in &quot;every power is equally good&quot;, but more that &quot;every power is viable&quot;. It also makes a lot of use of elements from the nWoD corebook. Ghosts are a significant presence in the setting, there are a myriad Affinities dealing with Derangements, Virtues, and Vices, and as a whole it feels like a tight, complete set of mechanics that nicely expand on the mortal rules. It's as if, just before the shift to the GMC and Second Edition, they actually managed to make a game line that works more or less perfectly in the old rules. I love virtually every game line in the World of Darkness excepting Werewolf and Mage (and Werewolf is just because I've never really looked into it), but the mechanics side of most of them have felt a bit of a mess. The second editions are helping them hit parity with Mummy, and using a new shiny ruleset that has people excited because new editions are always exciting. It does make me feel bad for Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T00:00:52-07:00","id":289300,"title":"","content":"While powers wise I did find some of the Utterances underpowered and putting aside of Egyptophilia and love of the CWoD Mummy games. Mummy captured the Weird Tales Lovecraftian feel of the NWoD more than other game lines did for me. It wasn't something I was expecting completely going on, even though dark pulp was one of the buzz words. A pleasant surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T04:22:21-07:00","id":289423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277992-development-tease-book-of-the-deceived?p=288869#post288869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it too late to get another spoiler out of the noble CAS?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your wish is my command.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/development-tease-the-deceived-mummy-the-curse/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/development-tease-the-deceived-mummy-the-curse/\" target=\"_blank\"> Development Tease: The Deceived [Mummy: 